WEBVTT

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.200
A 3,000-person capacity concert?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:19.620
"SEPTEMBER 22nd
HOLD A SOLO LIVE SHOW FOR 3,000 PEOPLE"

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.950
"SEPTEMBER 22nd
HOLD A SOLO LIVE SHOW FOR 3,000 PEOPLE"

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.950
Yes. That was the Order
the Wall spat out last night.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.620
Even though this will be a solo show,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.330
it's pushing a 3,000-person
capacity venue on you, too.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.330
Y-Yeah!

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.330
A solo show with 3,000 people?
Isn't that amazing?

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:42.330
3,000 people gives you the feeling
it's really an idol show!

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.700
Do you really think 3,000
people will come to see us?

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.250
Mr. Wall said they would,
so there's no doubt that they will!

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.620
That's true. So far, all of his Orders
have been right on the money.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.790
You could say he's a master tactician.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.370
"I knew my observations were correct!"

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.540
Why are they your observations, though?

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.200
The only thing Kono did was impulse buy.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.410
Isn't this amazing, Miu?

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.790
Yeah!

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.160
Well, I guess it's normal to be nervous, right?

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.660
Let's give our all in preparing
for this concert.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.620
Yeah!

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:54.790
"Dreaming Robot"

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.290
I've always wondered, just what is that?

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.910
It's my timecard.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.790
Since we're done today, I'm punching out.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.040
Huh? Time... what?

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.700
I believe it's important to firmly separate
your work life from your private life.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.870
Show-biz work is already disorderly as it is.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.790
If you separate the two,
you can concentrate on your work more.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.660
It's the rational choice.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.700
Rational, huh?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.290
That being said, good work today.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.950
"WE ARE CLOSED FOR TODAY."

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.950
Yeah, you, too.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.330
Thank you for your hard work today.
Excuse me.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.370
Wow, Akane is always so punctual.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.910
As an idol, though, she's a bit stiff.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:47.540
I really have no clue
why she decided to be an idol.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.040
That's true.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.080
There definitely has to be some kind
of grand or noble reason as to why.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.120
That reminds me.
Something has been worrying me.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.410
I've heard something before...

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.000
...about someone named Akane Maruyama.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.700
Huh.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.250
It happened a long time ago,
but I remember somewhere...

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.700
"9 YEARS AGO"

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.750
"ATELIER SHIRUKURO"

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.910
Whoa! Great! That's so good, Akane!

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.750
Listen to me, Akane!
Entertainment is about emotion,

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.620
an explosion of emotion,

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.040
so let your passion guide you,
and let your paintbrush roam free!

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.120
I didn't even think of that!

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.250
You're amazing, Akane!

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.450
Are you okay, Akane?

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.830
I'm gonna become an idol!

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.160
You were messing around at the atelier again?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:32.000
Akane! You promised that you were
going to do your homework today!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.250
But it isn't even interesting.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.910
Whether or not it's interesting
isn't the problem!

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:40.250
Now, now. It seems
she does have some remorse about--

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.160
And you're always spoiling her
by saying things like that!

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.950
You're not just moody, but self-indulgent, too!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.080
In the next era, girls are going to have
to stand out even more on their own!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.290
Now, now, I don't think it's that--

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:54.410
Are you even listening, Akane?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.750
I hate Mom!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.330
She probably doesn't even care about me!

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:05.330
That can't be right.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.540
She's just thinking
about things for your future.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.540
Nope, still hate her.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:15.370
Surely there will come a day when you'll
understand what your mother is telling you.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.540
But more importantly...

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.620
...when you mentioned becoming an idol,
you weren't serious.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.830
I was.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.790
No, I'll become an astronaut instead!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.120
--Please note, we will be doing bag checks today
here onsite before the show begins.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.250
--Please line up right here!
--Please note, we will be doing bag checks today
here onsite before the show begins.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.500
"THIS IS THE END OF THE LINE"

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.500
This is the end of the line!

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.250
Step right up!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.410
--Um, I'd like a penlight,
a Nicorun muffler towel, and a T-shirt.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.250
--So you'd like four things, correct?
--Um, I'd like a penlight,
a Nicorun muffler towel, and a T-shirt.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.950
"CONGRATS ON YOUR CONCERT,
EVERYONE IN 22/7!
FROM YOUR FANS."

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.000
"CONGRATULATIONS
MISS MIU TAKIGAWA,
FROM YOUR FANS."

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.410
"CONGRATULATIONS, 22/7!
FROM EVERYONE AT WEEKLY
SHONEN MONDAY MAGAZINE"

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.870
"CONGRATULATIONS 22/7,
MISSES MIYAKO KONO AND JUN TODA,
FROM EVERYONE AT FM73 NAMINAMI EGG"

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:54.080
That's it for the rehearsal.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.660
For the actual show...

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.950
We look forward to working with you!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.120
Yay!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.250
Hey. You're going to become
a bother to the venue staff,

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:11.200
so hurry and go back to the green room!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.200
Oh, no. My butt's gonna get spanked!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.200
Now, now. We're allowed to do
this sort of thing for a concert like this.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.950
Gets everyone more excited, right?

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:22.450
And, you, don't just laze around!

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:32.660
What's this?
Are we a bit nervous, Nicole?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.870
Stop messing around. Who's nervous?

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.290
But...

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:43.120
I absolutely want
to make this concert a success.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.540
Right!

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:45.580
So let's do our best!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:46.660
Yeah!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.830
Wow! This is so cool!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.620
It's a nice place, right?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.410
Makes me want to sketch the hill nearby.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:05.910
Hey, Akane! We didn't come here to play!

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.790
Akane, your father forgot something,
and I'm going to go bring it to him.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:21.870
You're not to leave this house.
Stay right where you are.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.250
We're pretty deep here in the mountains.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.500
"MARIA AND THE MAGIC PICTURE BOOK"

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.500
We're pretty deep here in the mountains.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.950
"MARIA AND THE MAGIC PICTURE BOOK"

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.950
Got it!

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.910
"MOUNTAIN PEAK"
"TRAILHEAD"

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.620
Sheesh!

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:42.290
How can I be expected to stay in the house
when we've come to such a fun place?

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:46.160
Wherever I go, I can get back by using
the path I took to get there in the first place.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.870
So it's not like I can get lost--

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.750
Ow.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.660
"BREAKING NEWS
300 PEOPLE SEARCHING IN THE MOUNTAINS"
"LITTLE AKANE HAS GONE MISSING
KITAMI MOUNTAINS"

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:13.250
"BREAKING NEWS
300 PEOPLE SEARCHING IN THE MOUNTAINS"

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:13.250
It has been roughly three days
since little Akane Maruyama

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:18.540
"LITTLE AKANE HAS GONE MISSING
KITAMI MOUNTAINS"

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:18.540
has gotten lost here
in the Kitami Mountains in Hokkaido.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:23.290
Local police and a rescue party
have been searching for her day and night,

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.580
but finding her is becoming very unlikely.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.950
--Akane!
--Akane!

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.750
--Hey!
--Akane!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.950
Akane!

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:35.120
We searched the west roads,
but couldn't find her.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.080
"KITAMI MOUNTAINS FIRE DEPARTMENT
SEARCH PARTY HEADQUARTERS"

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.080
We've widened the search,
and we still don't have any clues.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:40.950
Our investigation shows a possibility
that she slipped and fell.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.910
I'm so hungry.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:58.620
I want to eat Mom's meat loaf.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.790
I wonder if I'm going to die at this rate.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:23.160
Akane.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:31.750
Mom!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.500
Were you here... the whole time?

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.660
Yeah.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.830
For the past three days?

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.080
Yeah.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.540
It's my fault, because I went and got lost!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.830
You even told me, Mom...

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.000
...that I should stay in the house!

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.120
Akane!

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:01.160
I'm so glad.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:15.580
But it didn't just end there.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.200
"LITTLE GIRL RECOVERED SAFELY"

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.200
The little girl who went missing
near her lodgings...

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.750
At the same time, it was viewed
by the world as a miraculous play,

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:22.620
"A MIRACULOUS RESCUE!"

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:22.620
At the same time, it was viewed
by the world as a miraculous play,

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.330
"FOUND SAFELY"

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.330
gathering a huge crowd
of people.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:23.790
"IT'S A MIRACLE!
AKANE HAS BEEN FOUND!"

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:23.790
gathering a huge crowd
of people.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.500
"A MOTHER PREPARED FOR DEATH"

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.500
gathering a huge crowd
of people.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.620
Even at that time, you were...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.870
Haven't we talked enough about this?

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:31.450
--The only reason why Akane was acting up
was because you were so harsh with her!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.370
--This incident provided my parents
--The only reason why Akane was acting up
was because you were so harsh with her!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:39.330
--with the perfect chance to fight
with each other as much as they could.
--Shut the hell up! I only had to
because all you did was spoil her!

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.450
The weekly tabloids reported about that.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.250
"WAS THAT SEVEN-YEAR-OLD CHILD
ABANDONED IN THE MOUNTAINS?
THE TRUTH BEHIND THE MIRACULOUS RESCUE
AND AN ARTIST'S HOUSE OF DARKNESS."

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:45.700
That touching story turned into gossip.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.790
Finally they got a divorce.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.000
"MARIA AND THE MAGIC PICTURE BOOK"

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.000
Finally they got a divorce.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.330
"MARIA AND THE MAGIC PICTURE BOOK"

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.330
My mom was right about everything
from the start.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.540
I should have stayed put in that cabin!

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:23.540
My moodiness and capriciousness
were wounded by my family.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:27.790
If I were to become emotional,
it would lead to someone's misfortune.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.200
And so, I...

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.040
"AKANE"

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:38.790
I just transferred here.
My name is Akane Maruyama.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.120
I look forward to learning with you all.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.160
I'm starting to get nervous.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.080
Piano! Piano! Wait! There's no piano!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.290
Someone go get Miu a piano!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.700
Where'd you leave your pride as an idol?

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.080
You're just brimming
with the need to help people again.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.950
Aren't you nervous, Akane?

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.870
That's because Akane is a robot.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.500
Yes, yes, that's right.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.000
Wow, she's just openly admitting it.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.540
Wh-What are you making me eat?

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.000
Human!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.620
In Japan, when you're nervous,
you eat a "human," right?

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.080
Don't make it sound like we're cannibals!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.870
You're supposed to eat it yourself!

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.700
Since she started a little bit ago,
Toda's eaten about 30 people.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.700
She really is a cannibal!

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.410
Stop flailing! Everything is fine.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.200
We're not beginners anymore, right?

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.540
That's true. We've done all we can, too.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.660
S-Surely...

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.830
Surely, I think we'll be able
to put on a wonderful show.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.750
That's right. We just have to be confident!

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.250
Yeah! Let's get pumped!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.870
Okay, here we go.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:04.950
Is everyone ready?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.870
--Wheat flour!
--Pork!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.830
Cabbage!

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:11.830
Chinese yam!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:12.910
Tenkasu!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:13.910
Pickled ginger!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:14.910
Dried shrimp!

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.000
Eggs.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.080
Just flip it over!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.660
22/7!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:47.660
--♪ Just by having someone nearby ♪

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:48.370
--Mew-Mew!
--♪ Just by having someone nearby ♪

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.450
--♪ Makes me feel like I can't breathe ♪

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.250
--Nicorun!
--♪ Makes me feel like I can't breathe ♪

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:55.290
--♪ I can't live alone ♪

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.120
--Akane!
--♪ I can't live alone ♪

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.080
--♪ Understanding that I still feel depressed ♪

00:14:59.080 --> 00:14:59.750
--Reika!
--♪ Understanding that I still feel depressed ♪

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.790
--♪ Even if you don't come talk to me ♪

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:03.540
--Sakura!
--♪ Even if you don't come talk to me ♪

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.540
--♪ As if someone were being considerate of me ♪

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:07.290
--Jun-Jun!
--♪ As if someone were being considerate of me ♪

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.250
--♪ With things like warmth and kindness ♪

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.120
--Ayaka!
--♪ With things like warmth and kindness ♪

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:14.200
--♪ I find myself exhausted from love ♪

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:14.870
--Mya-ko!
--♪ I find myself exhausted from love ♪

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.870
♪ And in my annoyance ♪

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:22.500
♪ My annoyance, I ask ♪

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.330
♪ What are you looking for? ♪

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:26.330
♪ What are you refusing? ♪

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:30.750
♪ I have no choice but to leave ♪

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.790
♪ Don't close the door, don't slam the door ♪

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:39.330
♪ Leave it but one centimeter open ♪

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.040
♪ And as hazy light spills through that gap ♪

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:48.120
♪ Please leave me a way home ♪

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.870
Even though you've been so wounded,

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.250
I wonder why you won't reject me?

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.120
That is why I fall into self-loathing.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.160
♪ One day, I will realize ♪

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:01.200
♪ That by my side ♪

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:04.830
♪ I had an empathizer like none other ♪

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:52.160
I can hear my voice.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.790
I can hear the audience.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.160
I can hear everyone's voices.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.910
All of our fans are right here.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.120
And I'm right here.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.910
Right now, in this moment...

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:08.250
We are all one!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.080
I really thought my heart was gonna stop!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:33.200
I think that's the most nervous
I've ever been so far.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.750
Would it be okay to have a snack?

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.160
You'll get fat.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.830
Replacing calories!

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:40.750
But...

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:44.000
That was fun, wasn't it?

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:50.580
22/7! 22/7!

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:52.000
Wha--

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.250
--Is this...
--22/7! 22/7!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.830
--An encore?
--22/7! 22/7!

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.450
--22/7! 22/7!

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:59.540
--This is the first time!
--22/7! 22/7!

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.370
--Yeah. Yeah!
--22/7! 22/7!

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:21.660
Akane!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:23.910
Huh?

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.040
She's crying. Akane's crying!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.620
Our AI!

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.580
I wonder...

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.910
...if it's because I was so happy?

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:40.620
That's not fair!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.410
If Akane makes me start crying,
I won't be able to stop!

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.870
That ain't fair!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:51.370
Akane!
You're not a robot after all!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:54.290
Akane, everyone...

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:56.620
Let's go!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.000
Akane, let's go.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:04.950
Yes.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:08.330
Let's make this the best encore!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.660
Yeah!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:22.950
I don't really like myself
or the fact that I'm an idol very much.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:28.660
I have yet to find an answer
as to why I keep singing and dancing.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.370
But there's one thing I do know.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.410
And that is...

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:39.750
I love 22/7!

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.580
The reason I became an idol?

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.500
Because it's close to my house,
and it allows me to get exercise.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.370
Is that right?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.830
"WEEKLY SHONEN
MONDAY MAGAZINE"

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.370
Anyway, let's talk about last night's concert.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:02.450
When you heard the 3,000 fans chanting,
were you moved by that?

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:06.290
Not really.
I just did what I was supposed to do as usual.

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:12.620
Um, well, I heard about you crying
from your other group members.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:16.910
Well, the definition of me crying
is more on a metaphysical level.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.660
Now then, it's time.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.790
Ah, right...

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.830
Thank you very much.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.040
She's so punctual.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.790
Amazing! It's so big!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:16.160
Who knew that the office
had something like this?

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:19.450
Oh, it's so nice.

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.450
Wow, sentou style!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:25.620
It really is a bathhouse.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.410
Akane's here, too!

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.580
What?

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:08.450
Miu!

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:10.660
Sakura!

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.160
Welcome!

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.370
Was everything okay with your Mom?
Did she oppose you moving in?

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:17.370
A bit.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:23.290
Well, that makes sense!
But I'm so happy now that you can sleep over.

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:24.330
Yeah.

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:27.660
Okay! I'll help you carry stuff!

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:29.370
Th-Thanks.

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.160
Saito!

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:37.120
S-So close.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:41.830
You've changed.

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:47.370
Or maybe you haven't changed after all.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:50.540
Hey, Mew-Mew!

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:57.410
The commuter gang is all here,
so tonight we're gonna have a party!

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:06.410
All right.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:10.000
"Episode 9: Lullaby of the Stars"

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.950
"Episode 9: Lullaby of the Stars"

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.950
"Lullaby of the Stars."
